  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>Tokenized stocks distributed value rose 17.5% over 30D:</strong> Tokenized equity distributed value at $3.23B (17.5% higher over 30D) shows the early lane still adding balance sheet on a small set of platforms. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/podcasts-and-videos/podcast/synthetic-vs-direct-tokenized-stocks-who-wins-after-the-sec-exemption\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Synthetic vs. Direct Tokenized Stocks: Who Wins After The SEC Exemption?</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Tokenized stocks remain an early-stage lane:</strong> liquidity and scale are still concentrated in a small set of platforms/networks. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/converge/tradfi-and-fintech/tokenized-stock-holder-count-reaches-4-3-million-led-by-bnb-chain\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tokenized-Stock Holder Count Reaches 4.3 Million, Led by BNB Chain</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Tokenized equities remain an early access market:</strong> Liquidity and scale stay concentrated until broker distribution and custody plumbing can support broader trading. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/09/29/cboe-s-and-p-dow-jones-may-explore-tokenized-options-contracts-under-extended-licensing-deal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cboe, S&amp;P Dow Jones may explore tokenized options contracts under extended licensing deal</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Securities and broker-rule constraints often set the pace more than listing count, so near-term share stays tied to venues that can actually distribute products. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/markets/2026-09-30-clarity-acts-failure-gave-crypto-faster-regulatory-wins-bitwise-says-417362\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Clarity Act\u2019s failure gave crypto \u2018faster\u2019 regulatory wins, Bitwise CIO says</a> (The Block).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
